      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2017 Teng et al.",
        "AbstractText": "Streptococcus suis, a zoonotic bacterium found primarily in pigs, has been recognized recently as an emerging pathogen of humans. Herein, we describe the genome of Streptococcus suis strain SC19, a hypervirulent and vaccine candidate strain isolated from a pig amid the 2005 outbreak in China."
